---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How it works" description="From a 15-minute chat to a live website in about a week, then same-day changes by WhatsApp. Here’s exactly how Running Tab works.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1>From chat to live in about a week</h1>
      <p class="lead">You run the venue. We run the website. Here’s what happens, step by step, and what we need from you, which isn’t much.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px"><div class="step-num">1</div><h3>A 15-minute chat</h3><p>At your venue during a quiet spell, or on the phone. We ask how people find you, how they book, and what’s annoying you about your current setup. No sales pitch marathon.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px"><div class="step-num">2</div><h3>A free homepage mockup (within 2 working days)</h3><p>We put together a draft homepage using your name, your menu and your photos from Instagram or Google, so you can see exactly what you’d get. If it’s not for you, no hard feelings.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px"><div class="step-num">3</div><h3>We build your site (about 5 working days)</h3>
        <p>You send us a few things and we do the rest:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your logo, if you have one, and 10–20 photos (phone photos are fine)</li>
          <li>Your current menu: a photo of the board is fine</li>
          <li>Opening hours, booking link, and any events or private-hire details</li>
          <li>Access to your domain, if you have one. We’ll help you find it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We move over everything worth keeping from your old site, and connect your existing booking system.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px"><div class="step-num">4</div><h3>You approve, then you pay</h3><p>Nothing is charged until you’ve seen the finished site and said yes. Then we put it live, check Google has your correct hours, and set up your monthly tab.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="step-num">5</div><h3>Text us changes, any time</h3><p>New menu, a holiday closure, an event on Friday? Send it by WhatsApp or email. On Core it’s done within 1 working day. On Plus, menu, hours and closure changes sent before 3pm are done the same day, 7 days a week. Each month you get a short note saying what we changed and that everything’s healthy.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow">
      <h2>What counts as a “change”?</h2>
      <p>One request about content on a page you already have: a new menu (even the whole thing), new prices, new hours, swapping photos, adding an event, a “Closed Boxing Day” banner, or a text update of up to about 300 words. Several small changes in one message usually count as one.</p>
      <p>New pages, new features and redesigns are extras. See the add-ons on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.</p>
      <h2 style="margin-top:1.5em">Do you use AI?</h2>
      <p>Yes, honestly. We use modern tools, including AI, to build sites quickly and make your changes fast. That’s how we keep the price at £49. A real person checks every change before it goes live, and you can always talk to a human.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Book a free chat</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
